Changes to OCCT (V8_0_1) for the Open CAD Viewer. Applied by wasm/scripts/build-occt.sh.

- STEP AP242 external element references and assembly instance paths (CAx-IF External (Element)
  References 3.1, section 7; PMI 4.1, section 9.3.4; User Defined Attributes 1.8, section 6.2):
  - Read MULTI_LEVEL_REFERENCE_DESIGNATOR (830), COMPONENT_PATH_SHAPE_ASPECT (831),
    EXTERNALLY_DEFINED_REPRESENTATION_ITEM (832), EXTERNALLY_DEFINED_ITEM_WITH_MULTIPLE_REFERENCES
    (833) and SHAPE_REPRESENTATION_REFERENCE (834) with new classes, and register the existing
    StepBasic_ProductDefinitionReference (828) and ..WithLocalRepresentation (829) classes, which
    had read/write tools but were never recognised: an assembly whose externally defined part is a
    PRODUCT_DEFINITION_REFERENCE_WITH_LOCAL_REPRESENTATION lost that part.
  - EXTERNALLY_DEFINED_REPRESENTATION was read as a plain representation (3 parameters) and failed
    on its 5; it now reads, writes and keeps item_id and source.
  - Assembly PMI: a GD&T object (or a presentation) whose shape aspect is a
    component_path_shape_aspect references the faces of the component's shape aspect, in this
    file or, through an EXTERNAL_ANCHOR in the header of the component's file, in another. Usages
    whose parent is a part in another file are resolved there by reference designator. The
    instance each reference is on is kept: STEPCAFControl_Reader::GetGDTAssemblyReferences (the
    assembly, the component labels down to the instance, the sub-shape labels).
  - User-defined attributes on a multi_level_reference_designator go on the SHUO of the instance.

